# Mandatory mission timing

For every implementation, investigation, validation, deployment, repair, or
documentation mission:

## At the beginning

Before running the first implementation command or modifying any file, execute:

```bash
TASK_TIMING_FILE="$(git rev-parse --git-path appsolino-task-timing.env)"
mkdir -p "$(dirname "$TASK_TIMING_FILE")"

TASK_START_UTC="$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
TASK_START_EPOCH="$(date +%s)"

printf 'TASK_START_UTC=%q\nTASK_START_EPOCH=%q\n' \
  "$TASK_START_UTC" \
  "$TASK_START_EPOCH" \
  > "$TASK_TIMING_FILE"

printf 'TASK_STARTED_UTC=%s\n' "$TASK_START_UTC"
```

Do not infer the start time later from commits, logs, prompts, or file
timestamps.

## At completion or stop

After the final validation and before writing the final report, execute:

```bash
TASK_TIMING_FILE="$(git rev-parse --git-path appsolino-task-timing.env)"

if [[ -f "$TASK_TIMING_FILE" ]]; then
  source "$TASK_TIMING_FILE"

  TASK_END_UTC="$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
  TASK_END_EPOCH="$(date +%s)"
  TASK_DURATION_SECONDS=$((TASK_END_EPOCH - TASK_START_EPOCH))

  TASK_DURATION_HOURS=$((TASK_DURATION_SECONDS / 3600))
  TASK_DURATION_MINUTES=$(((TASK_DURATION_SECONDS % 3600) / 60))
  TASK_DURATION_REMAINING_SECONDS=$((TASK_DURATION_SECONDS % 60))

  printf -v TASK_DURATION \
    '%02dh %02dm %02ds' \
    "$TASK_DURATION_HOURS" \
    "$TASK_DURATION_MINUTES" \
    "$TASK_DURATION_REMAINING_SECONDS"

  printf 'TASK_STARTED_UTC=%s\n' "$TASK_START_UTC"
  printf 'TASK_ENDED_UTC=%s\n' "$TASK_END_UTC"
  printf 'TASK_WALL_CLOCK_DURATION=%s\n' "$TASK_DURATION"

  rm -f "$TASK_TIMING_FILE"
else
  TASK_END_UTC="$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
  TASK_DURATION="TIMING_NOT_RECORDED"

  printf 'TASK_STARTED_UTC=TIMING_NOT_RECORDED\n'
  printf 'TASK_ENDED_UTC=%s\n' "$TASK_END_UTC"
  printf 'TASK_WALL_CLOCK_DURATION=TIMING_NOT_RECORDED\n'
fi
```

## Required final report fields

Every final report must contain:

```text
Task started UTC:
Task ended UTC:
Wall-clock duration:
Long interruption or pause:
```

Rules:

* Report actual wall-clock duration, not the expected estimate.
* Do not invent a missing start time.
* When timing was not started correctly, report `TIMING_NOT_RECORDED`.
* Record interruptions longer than 15 minutes separately.
* Stop timing only after validation and cleanup are complete.
